  "stop_note": "K1 line 6b49dd94 (c): the bucket no longer serves the files. The listing answered 403 AccessDenied (patentsview#14); g_patent.tsv.zip answered 403 AccessDenied (chunk patentsview#15, manifest #16), so the two assignee files were not asked. USPTO notice of 2026-03-18 (patentsview#17): PatentsView migrated to the Open Data Portal on 2026-03-20, its data downloads available through ODP; USPTO PatentsView page (patentsview#18): granted patents through 2025-12-31 as the ODP dataset pvgpatdis (data.uspto.gov/bulkdata/datasets/pvgpatdis). The portal serves its app page to this client (patentsview#4, #7) and its API takes a key, so no other route was tried: the inbox block of 2026-10-25 names the choices. No byte of a grant or assignee table is held.",
  "requests_this_sitting": "patentsview#1-#18: robots and home (#1-#4), USPTO robots and terms (#5, #6), the portal bundle (#7), Wayback index and snapshots (#8-#13), the listing (#14), g_patent (#15, #16), the notice and page (#17, #18); /bin/bash",
  "sitting_2": {
   "date": "2026-10-25",
   "ruling": "the operator's (d) of D551, \"a browser read first\" (drop file patents-browser.md, relayed 10-25 ~19:48 ET), applied on feature/fx-spot-proposer-1",
   "k1_line": "a4b7afd8 (main, mirror-pushed before any read): data.uspto.gov in place of 6b49dd94's bucket; the dataset page by the probe's browser transport under b373ed8a (2), (3)",
   "build": "e75454fa (main, mirror-pushed before the read): data.uspto.gov and 0dd6fc7fe1e2.edge.sdk.awswaf.com on ADMITTED_READ, section 368; RD.67 test first, two mutants fail it, root chain rc 0",
   "run": "node scripts/probe-chokepoints-c5.mjs 368, once (log /var/tmp/patents-s1/run-368.log)",
   "rows": {
    "waf_robots": "patentsview#19 (HTTP 404: open)",
    "portal_robots": "patentsview#20 (HTTP 200, the app page: no robots file, admitted by ADMITTED_READ)",
    "page": "patentsview#21 (HTTP 200, the 20,666-byte app page)",
    "bundles": "patentsview#22-#34 (main, polyfills, scripts and 10 chunks: each HTTP 200 text/html, the same 20,666 bytes as #4)",
    "waf": "patentsview#35 (challenge.js, 686,413 B), #36 (mp_verify: a token, issued after the bundles were asked), #37 (telemetry)",
    "rendered": "patentsview#38 (21,006 B, no text in its body), #39 (the grab, 4,254 B)",
    "unanswered": [
     "https://data.uspto.gov/styles-75PCGEDN.css"
    ],
    "not_asked": 7
   },
   "finding": "The portal answers every path asked before its AWS WAF token is held with its app page, its own script bundles too, so one load renders nothing: the Angular app never starts and no dataset, file list or link is shown. The token (#36) comes from the page's WAF script after the bundles were asked; a second load in the same session would carry it, which the reader does not make (one load a read, no cookie kept past it). A file at data.uspto.gov asked by a plain request carries no token and gets the app page (patentsview#1-#7, #22-#34), and a browser's token carried into a plain request is item (6)'s 'a script that claims to be a browser it is not': K1 line a4b7afd8 (c), the route falls back to D551's (a).",
   "requests": "19 answers (#19-#37) and 1 unanswered, each through the reader behind ask's guard; 2 rendered rows (#38, #39); $0; no byte of a table held, no trial"
  },
  "stop_note_2": "K1 line a4b7afd8 (c): sitting 2's browser read of the pvgpatdis dataset page (section 368, patentsview#19-#39) rendered no file list: before its WAF token the portal serves its app page for every path, its scripts included. The route falls back to D551's (a), the operator's API key, as the inbox block of 2026-10-25 (sitting 2)."
 },
